  "summary": "A V-belt drive transmits power between parallel shafts by friction between wedge-shaped belts and grooved sheaves. The speed ratio equals the ratio of sheave diameters (here 2.5:1). Belts are tensioned by sliding the motor on its base; a guard protects people. Belt drives are simple, quiet, absorb shock and allow speed changes by changing sheaves.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Mechanical drive",
    "type": "Multi-groove classical/narrow V-belt drive"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "belts": 3,
    "ratio": "2.5:1",
    "tensioning": "Motor slide base with screw"
  },
